From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:45:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/72] DeepSeek settings: TF_DSV41_BIAS_VL is on whenever set,
 as its reader takes it

e17c6ff09 gave TF_DSV41_BIAS_VL a 0/1 flag row, but its one reader
(env_validate.imageBiasEnv) selects the vision bias for any non-blank text,
and the shipped default profile sets the checkpoint directory
(TF_DSV41_BIAS_VL=/model). Every boot of that profile stopped with
InvalidEnvironment before loading the model.

A new `present` kind takes any text without control characters as on (1),
blank or unset as off, so the row validates exactly what the reader uses.
Tests cover /model, 0, 1 and words selecting the bias and control
characters refusing; docs/profiles.md says the same.
---
 docs/profiles.md                              |  5 +++--
 .../deepseek_v41/env_startup_test.zig         |  4 ++--
 .../deepseek_v41/env_validate_test.zig        | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 zig/src/platform/environment.zig              | 10 +++++-----
 zig/src/platform/environment_test.zig         |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/profiles.md b/docs/profiles.md
index 52ca5bdd2d10c2b73a48d2d223716be6616ef264..7b52f7462d792fa0ae16e5094e9f6a7a1aa052d6 100644
--- a/docs/profiles.md
+++ b/docs/profiles.md
@@ -196,8 +196,9 @@ The table row, the batch reader and the planner use that list, and a host test k
 Every floor reader shares its row's space trim and named refusal. The hard floor has one reader in the KV budget,
 used by the pool, graph room, scheduler and prefill path; its unset value remains 4 GiB.
 
-`BIAS_VL` retains its accepted presence forms: unset/blank off, while both `0` and `1` select vision bias.
-Other text refuses. Engram queue depth remains 64 by default and permits 0 for serial reads. Reader threads
+`BIAS_VL` keeps its presence meaning: unset/blank is off, and any other text selects vision bias, including `0`,
+`1` and the checkpoint directory that shipped profiles name (`TF_DSV41_BIAS_VL=/model`); only control characters
+refuse. Engram queue depth remains 64 by default and permits 0 for serial reads. Reader threads
 remain 16 by default and accept 0 through 32; larger values refuse instead of clamping. Generation streams
 remain 1 by default.
 
